            <ArticleTitle>A capped trigonal pyramidal molybdenum hydrido complex and an unusually mild sulfur-carbon bond cleavage reaction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11032-11035</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06372e</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>DFT calculations reveal that a reported molybdenum hydride complex has an unprecedented geometry with the molybdenum in the base of trigonal pyramid defined by three thiolate ligands with a phosphine ligand on the apex and a hydride capping a PS2 face. This complex reacts with methanol to produce a sulfido complex by a new reaction: the protonation of an ipso carbon of a thiolate ligand by coordinated methanol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
